{
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Chapter 9: Peace on Paper",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s10b01",
     "shot": "accords",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "On January 27, 1973, the Paris Peace Accords were signed.",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       "w:signed.",
       0.5
      ]
     ],
     "date": 1973
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b02",
     "shot": "accords",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The agreement provided for a ceasefire, the withdrawal of American forces,",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:ceasefire,",
       0.4
      ],
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:withdrawal",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b03",
     "shot": "accords",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "and the return of American prisoners of war.",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop2",
       "w:prisoners",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b04",
     "shot": "homecoming",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "In the months that followed, American combat forces withdrew from Vietnam.",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "whoosh",
       4,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b05",
     "shot": "homecoming",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Hundreds of American prisoners returned home in Operation Homecoming.",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pops",
       "w:Hundreds",
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b06",
     "shot": "nobel",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Secretary of State Henry Kissinger and North Vietnamese negotiator Le Duc Tho received the",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "sparkle",
       "w:Kissinger",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b07",
     "shot": "nobel",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "1973 Nobel Peace Prize for their efforts toward ending the conflict.",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b08",
     "shot": "nobel",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Le Duc Tho declined the award, arguing that peace had not truly been achieved.",
     "date": 1973,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "hit",
       "w:declined",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b09",
     "shot": "point_peace",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "He had a point.",
     "date": null,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b10",
     "shot": "unresolved",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The agreement did not resolve the fundamental struggle over who would control South Vietnam.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b11",
     "shot": "unresolved",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "North Vietnamese troops remained in the South.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b12",
     "shot": "unresolved",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The South Vietnamese government continued to fight communist forces.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b13",
     "shot": "unresolved",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Both sides accused the other of violating the ceasefire.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:violating",
       0.5
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b14",
     "shot": "alone",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "And without American combat troops, South Vietnam faced a much more difficult military situation.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b15",
     "shot": "alone",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Washington had promised to support its ally, but American domestic politics had changed.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b16",
     "shot": "alone",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Congress was increasingly unwilling to fund another major American intervention.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "stamp",
       "w:unwilling",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b17",
     "shot": "alone",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "The United States had spent years fighting to prevent a communist victory in South Vietnam.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b18",
     "shot": "alone",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Now it was withdrawing.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "steps",
       4,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b19",
     "shot": "alone",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "And the question was whether the South Vietnamese government could survive on its own.",
     "date": 1974,
     "sfx": []
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b20",
     "shot": "clock",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "For a while, it did.",
     "date": null,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ticks",
       4,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s10b21",
     "shot": "clock",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "But the clock was ticking.",
     "date": null,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ticks",
       4,
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "mood": "curious"
  }
 ]
}